Apps on the desktop's dock.

An app adds itself by putting one JSON file here (or in /data/ark/apps):

  {"name": "FireFly", "icon": "firefly", "group": "Comms",
   "about": "Messages over LoRa and Wi-Fi",
   "exec": ["/home/ark/firefly/deploy/FireFly.sh"]}

name     shown on the dock (required)
exec     the program to start, with its arguments (required). A bare name
         is looked for on PATH and in /usr/games. While it runs,
         the desktop steps aside and comes back when the program ends. If the
         program is not there, the icon is dimmed ("not installed").
icon     one of: firefly stump ember sound chip video games  (app glyphs), or a window
         glyph (radar survey files network devices settings terminal update).
         Anything else: the first letter of the name.
group    groups and sorts the dock ("Comms", "Audio", ...).
about    one line, shown with the entry.
before   a command (list) run just before the app starts.
after    a command (list) run just after it exits. FireFly uses these to
         pause the Stump while it holds Reticulum's UDP port 29716.
mouse    false: the left stick is not a mouse while this app runs. Without
         it the app receives the stick as a mouse as well as a stick (R2 and
         L2 click, R1 and L1 are the wheel) and should use that or ignore it.
setup    a first-run setup screen built into the desktop (today: "stump").
needs    a file (or list) that exists once setup has run; until then the
         dock shows the entry as needing setup.

The app must draw with SDL2 (the desktop provides dArkOS's Mali driver and
SDL2 on LD_LIBRARY_PATH and sets SDL_VIDEODRIVER=kmsdrm), quit on
SELECT+START, and open the ALSA "default" device (not hw:0,0).

Full contract for builders: docs/building-apps.md in the RK3326 Linux repo.
